          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Zhou Enlai's Early Life</strong><br>\nZhou Enlai was born in 1898 in the town of Huai'an, Jiangsu province, China. He was raised by his uncle after his mother died when he was a child. Zhou excelled in school and was known for his intelligence and diligence. He went on to study in Japan and France, where he became involved in politics and the Chinese Communist movement.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Political Involvement in Youth</strong><br>\nDuring his time in Europe, Zhou Enlai was active in student movements and became a key member of the Chinese Communist Party (CCP). He helped organize labor strikes and was instrumental in spreading communist ideals. Zhou's leadership skills were recognized early on by his peers and by party leaders.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Return to China and Rise in the CCP</strong><br>\nAfter returning to China, Zhou quickly rose through the ranks of the CCP. He played a major role in the Northern Expedition, collaborating with the Nationalist Party to unite China under a central government. However, after the split between the Communists and Nationalists, Zhou worked to establish Communist bases in rural areas.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
