          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>The Long March</strong><br>\nZhou Enlai was a significant figure in the Long March, a strategic retreat of Communist forces in 1934-1935. He was responsible for negotiating with opposing forces and managed several key military operations. His leadership helped save the communist army from destruction and laid the groundwork for future successes.</p>\n\n<p><strong>World War II and the United Front</strong><br>\nDuring World War II, Zhou worked to establish a United Front with the Nationalists against Japan. His diplomatic skills were crucial in maintaining this precarious alliance. He was known for his ability to manage complex relationships and negotiate with various factions.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Founding of the People's Republic of China</strong><br>\nZhou played a vital part in the establishment of the People's Republic of China in 1949. As a trusted associate of Mao Zedong, he held several important government positions. Zhou's diplomatic talent was key in navigating the political landscape of the new government.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
