          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Premier of China</strong><br>\nAs the Premier of the People's Republic of China, Zhou Enlai was responsible for foreign policy and economic development. He worked to improve China's relationships with other countries and was often the face of China on the international stage. His policies helped to modernize China and improve the living standards of its people.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Cultural Revolution</strong><br>\nThe Cultural Revolution was a tumultuous time in China, and Zhou's position was often precarious. He attempted to moderate the excesses of the movement and protect many individuals, including intellectuals and former officials. His actions during this period preserved elements of the Chinese state and society.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Death and Legacy</strong><br>\nZhou Enlai died in 1976, and his death was widely mourned in China. He is remembered for his contributions to the Chinese revolution and his leadership as Premier. Zhou's political acumen and dedication to public service left a lasting impact on the history of modern China.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
